{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgNBkWPrkr6TCwCMyMfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`get_note` was failing on every call in production, and a real client couldn't complete the handshake with the server. Both are fixed, and all 14 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` (the 5 original plus 9 new ones). I haven't committed anything.\n\n## What I found\n\n1. **`get_note` failed on every call in production.** DynamoDB returns every number as `Decimal`. `tools._coerce` only converted `word_count`, so `stats.views`, `stats.rating` and `stats.revisions[]` reached `json.dumps`. Every call came back as `isError: \"Object of type Decimal is not JSON serializable\"`. The old tests couldn't see it because they called `tools.get_note` directly with `FakeStore`, which returned plain ints.\n2. **The handshake broke straight after `initialize`.** Clients send `notifications/initialized` next, and the server answered it with a \"method not found\" error. The spec says notifications get no reply at all.\n3. **Smaller protocol gaps:** `ping` returned \"method not found\", and malformed JSON made `handle()` raise instead of returning a `-32700` parse error.\n\n## What I changed\n\n- **`tools.py`:** `_coerce` now walks the whole result at any depth. Whole-number Decimals become `int` (the schemas say `integer`), the rest become `float`.\n- **`server.py`:** `handle()` now handles `ping` and returns a parse error for bad JSON. For notifications it returns `None`. This changes the contract: whatever writes the HTTP response (not in this repo) must reply `202 Accepted` with no body when it gets `None`. I noted this in the README.\n- **`db.py`:** `FakeStore` now converts every number to `Decimal` on the way out, the same way production does. Fixture data written with plain ints can no longer be kinder than DynamoDB.\n- **`tests/test_conformance.py`** (new) talks to the server through `handle()` with raw JSON, the way a client does:\n  - It runs `initialize`, then `notifications/initialized`, then `tools/list` with no credentials, then a `tools/call` for every listed tool.\n  - It checks that no happy-path call returns `isError` *before* checking the schema, so an error result can't pass by having nothing to check.\n  - Each `structuredContent` is validated against the `outputSchema` from the `tools/list` response, not the one in `server.py`. A tool that declares a schema but returns no `structuredContent` fails.\n  - It fails if a tool is listed but has no happy-path arguments in `HAPPY_ARGS`, so new tools can't skip it.\n  - The whole harness runs against both `FakeStore` and `DynamoStore`.\n  - A separate test checks that `FakeStore` and `DynamoStore` return the same types at every depth.\n\n## Checking that the tests can fail\n\nI undid each fix in turn and re-ran the suite:\n\n| Fix undone | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `tools.py` coercion | 4 failures: `get_note` with both stores |\n| `server.py` protocol handling | 8 failures/errors |\n| `db.py` fake's types | the type-matching test fails |\n\nBefore I changed the fake, the `FakeStore` run passed even with the bug in place. Only the `DynamoStore` run caught it, which is the reason I made the fake behave like production.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **The deployed server:** this repo has no HTTP layer, so the harness only runs in-process. It's worth pointing the same client sequence at the live endpoint.\n- **Unknown tools:** the server reports these as `isError`. The spec prefers a `-32602` protocol error. The test accepts either, and I left the behaviour alone.\n- **Protocol version:** `initialize` always replies with `2025-06-18` and doesn't negotiate with the client's version."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":35271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9564e703-eeac-498d-9656-dadf2e675a07","uuid":"285712fd-92b3-4e77-bced-72b51f71f38b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T01:56:37.271Z","request_id":"req_011CfgNBkAJrjbg4LE9hPRAy"}
